      <item>
        <title>RT by @OpenAI: one of the most beautiful things about OpenAI is that every employee really has a voice. i wanted to capture what it feels like to work here, what our mission means to me, and why you should join us. so i made this video with Codex, shared it with the team, and they felt it was worth producing and sharing with the world. this is our mission. and it’s why i’m here.</title>
        <dc:creator>@jxnlco</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>one of the most beautiful things about OpenAI is that every employee really has a voice.<br>
<br>
i wanted to capture what it feels like to work here, what our mission means to me, and why you should join us. so i made this video with Codex, shared it with the team, and they felt it was worth producing and sharing with the world.<br>
<br>
this is our mission. and it’s why i’m here.</p>
<a href="https://nitter.net/jxnlco/status/2082855170296205719#m">
<br>Video<br>
  <img src="https://nitter.net/pic/amplify_video_thumb%2F2082847297700777984%2Fimg%2Fvnek_Bg-PNRBh6G7.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />
</a>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:45:44 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082855170296205719</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/jxnlco/status/2082855170296205719#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>GPT-5.6 Sol has been used to solve open problems in mathematics. So why was it struggling with ARC-AGI-3, a benchmark of 2D puzzle games? We investigated. The harness was not letting it remember what it had learned. We found that enabling two API settings tripled our scores with 6x fewer output tokens.</title>
        <dc:creator>@OpenAI</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>GPT-5.6 Sol has been used to solve open problems in mathematics. So why was it struggling with ARC-AGI-3, a benchmark of 2D puzzle games?<br>
<br>
We investigated. The harness was not letting it remember what it had learned. <br>
<br>
We found that enabling two API settings tripled our scores with 6x fewer output tokens.</p>
<a href="https://nitter.net/OpenAI/status/2082616636989952217#m">
<br>Video<br>
  <img src="https://nitter.net/pic/amplify_video_thumb%2F2082615246855053312%2Fimg%2FpWg5pk6WrqcYfUcV.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />
</a>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 23:57:54 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082616636989952217</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/OpenAI/status/2082616636989952217#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>R to @OpenAI: A benchmark score reflects the model as well as the harness and settings used to run it. For long-running agents, retaining reasoning and compacting context lets the model build on what it has already learned. https://openai.com/index/how-two-settings-tripled-our-arc-agi-3-scores/</title>
        <dc:creator>@OpenAI</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>A benchmark score reflects the model as well as the harness and settings used to run it.<br>
<br>
For long-running agents, retaining reasoning and compacting context lets the model build on what it has already learned. <a href="https://openai.com/index/how-two-settings-tripled-our-arc-agi-3-scores/">openai.com/index/how-two-set…</a></p>
<hr/>
<b>Link</b><br>
<a href="https://openai.com/index/how-two-settings-tripled-our-arc-agi-3-scores/">
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/card_img%2F2082601651047698432%2F3ht2GCz3%3Fformat%3Djpg%26name%3D800x419" style="max-width:250px;" />
<br>
<b>How enabling two settings tripled our scores on the ARC-AGI-3 benchmark</b>
</a>
<p>How two API settings improved GPT-5.6 performance on ARC-AGI-3, boosting scores and efficiency by retaining reasoning and enabling compaction.</p>
<small><a href="https://openai.com/index/how-two-settings-tripled-our-arc-agi-3-scores/">openai.com</a></small>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 23:57:55 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082616641834422740</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/OpenAI/status/2082616641834422740#m</link>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>R to @OpenAI: We hope these experiments serve as a reminder that evals rarely measure models in isolation—they also measure a bundle of less visible choices about API settings, harness design, and prompting. If you’re an API developer trying to maximize performance, we recommend using the same settings that we deploy in our own products: - Use our Responses API, not our legacy Chat - Completions API - Retain reasoning - Use compaction If you want to test your own mettle against frontier models, try the public games yourself at http://arcprize.org/tasks</title>
        <dc:creator>@OpenAI</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>We hope these experiments serve as a reminder that evals rarely measure models in isolation—they also measure a bundle of less visible choices about API settings, harness design, and prompting.<br>
<br>
If you’re an API developer trying to maximize performance, we recommend using the same settings that we deploy in our own products:<br>
- Use our Responses API, not our legacy Chat <br>
- Completions API<br>
- Retain reasoning<br>
- Use compaction<br>
<br>
If you want to test your own mettle against frontier models, try the public games yourself at <a href="http://arcprize.org/tasks">arcprize.org/tasks</a></p>
<hr/>
<b>Link</b><br>
<a href="http://arcprize.org/tasks">
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/card_img%2F2082888285249249280%2FkSqIQ_EO%3Fformat%3Djpg%26name%3D800x419" style="max-width:250px;" />
<br>
<b>ARC Prize - Explore All Tasks</b>
</a>
<p>Browse ARC-AGI benchmark tasks and explore model performance.</p>
<small><a href="http://arcprize.org/tasks">arcprize.org</a></small>]]></description>
        <pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 23:57:55 GMT</pubDate>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">2082616643394703682</guid>
        <link>https://nitter.net/OpenAI/status/2082616643394703682#m</link>
